[{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268318136,"data":"# Kaggle kernel agent guide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268468184,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268476586,"data":"This file travels inside every kernel that `scripts/kaggle_run.py` pushes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268482072,"data":"and is printed at the top of its log. The repository's root AGENTS.md owns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268487028,"data":"every rule; this guide states what a Kaggle kernel is for, what it runs on,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268491231,"data":"and what it must prove before its output counts.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268495202,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268498962,"data":"## What runs where\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268502775,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268506561,"data":"| Substrate | Runs | Never runs |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268510421,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268514322,"data":"| Kaggle CPU kernel (the default) | every simulation of 14 qubits or fewer whose widest density matrix stays below 12 qubits (8 with mid-circuit measurement) | IBM jobs; anything needing an IBM credential |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268520681,"data":"| Kaggle GPU kernel (Aer on GPU, `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4`) | simulations whose widest density matrix reaches 12 qubits, or 8 with mid-circuit measurement (docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md, \"CPU against T4\") | IBM jobs; narrow replays, which the T4 speeds up by at most 3 times |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268525626,"data":"| Kaggle CPU in the same kernel | transpilation, package builds, the hypercomplex table extraction | |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268529692,"data":"| Kaggle TPU (`TpuV5E8`, `TpuV6E8`) | JAX code only; Aer has no TPU backend. An account without Persona identity verification gets a 4-core CPU machine for every TPU request; a verified account's request queues for a TPU, one batch session at a time (docs/notes/kaggle/tpu-research.md) | Qiskit or Aer |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268534578,"data":"| Kaggle Gemma models (attached through `model_sources`) | text tasks on request | evidence: a language-model answer supports no physical or mathematical claim |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268538902,"data":"| A 15-qubit run (decision-gated) | the substrate an approved written case names: Kaggle T4 x2 or build host Aer, a GPU state wider than one T4 cache-blocked across both (`calibration_snapshot.blocking_options`; docs/notes/kaggle/gpu-runbook.md), or Tuna-17 through Quantum Inspire, whose `submit` refuses while another session's hardware job is live | any substrate the case does not name |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26854647,"data":"| IBM Heron r2 (ibm_fez, ibm_kingston, ibm_marrakesh) | 16 or more qubits, or a question about a named device qubit, only after the owner approves a written case | simulations |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268569563,"data":"| GitHub Actions CPU | the CPU replay gate that re-derives a reduced case of each Kaggle result | GPU work |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268574777,"data":"| Build host (Arch, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB; guide in the untracked `docs/local/`) | development, dry runs, calibration exports, CPU replays, the Arch-packaged hypercomplex stack and SageMath | runs the routing rule sends to Kaggle |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268579735,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268583838,"data":"## Every kernel's phases\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26858838,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268593101,"data":"`kaggle_kernel/kernel_main.py` writes one JSON file per phase into\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268605435,"data":"`/kaggle/working/output`:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268609877,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268613583,"data":"1. `environment.json`: Python and package versions, CPU model and cores,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268617673,"data":"   RAM, working disk, every GPU (name, memory, driver, compute capability),\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268621575,"data":"   CUDA driver version, TPU devices, Aer devices, the Aer device the entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268625733,"data":"   runs on (`entry_aer_device`) and attached models.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268629593,"data":"2. `hypercomplex.json`: the hypercomplex stack, built and proved by\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268633611,"data":"   `scripts/algebra_package_tables.py`. `--fetch` downloads the seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268637581,"data":"   archives `RELEASES` pins and keeps each only if its sha256 matches.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268641698,"data":"   `--install` installs sixteen of them with `pip install --no-deps`,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268645412,"data":"   applying `BUILD_RECIPES` (the cayley-dickson, SplitOct and pyquaternion\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268649218,"data":"   PKGBUILD `prepare()` steps) and taking the Octonion-Sedenion wheel as\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268652798,"data":"   published, then installs `RUNTIME_PINS`: numpy-quaternion, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268662749,"data":"   seventeenth, as its pinned compiled wheel, and numba, sparse and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268666575,"data":"   anywidget. `--extract` binds all seventeen\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268670277,"data":"   installed distributions to their archives and regenerates\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268673956,"data":"   `docs/evidence/algebra_packages/tables.json`; the kernel stops with exit\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268677899,"data":"   code 3 unless those bytes equal the retained ones. The build host passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268681753,"data":"   the same test against its Arch packages, so a run that reaches its entry\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268685639,"data":"   used the same algebra code as the host. The file's `packages` field\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268690396,"data":"   records the versions `kernel_main.REPORTED_PACKAGES` names, nine of the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268695292,"data":"   seventeen algebra distributions; the byte comparison binds the rest.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268699909,"data":"3. `capacity.json` (smoke kernels): the widest GHZ circuit each Aer method\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268705222,"data":"   runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268709707,"data":"4. The entry's stdout and stderr, written to `stdout.txt` and `stderr.txt`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268713557,"data":"   as the entry prints (`kernel_main.start_entry` sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268718282,"data":"   `PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1`), then its exit code and the repository files it\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268722369,"data":"   changed, which the kernel copies under `repo/` after the entry exits.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268726281,"data":"   A session Kaggle ends at `--timeout` still returns\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268730223,"data":"   `/kaggle/working/output` but never reaches that copy, so an entry that\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268735033,"data":"   may outlive its timeout writes its record to an absolute path under\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268744635,"data":"   `/kaggle/working/output` and rewrites it after every finished unit of\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268748818,"data":"   work, as `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py` does per row.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268752712,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268756385,"data":"## Package stack\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268760175,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268763839000002,"data":"| Package | Pin | Kernel source |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268769624,"data":"| --- | --- | --- |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26879188,"data":"| qiskit | 2.6.0 | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268797212,"data":"| qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 | 0.17.2 (the CUDA 12 `qiskit-aer-gpu` stops at 0.15.1 and has no Python 3.13 wheel) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268802081,"data":"| cuquantum-cu11 | 24.8.0 (brings custatevec-cu11 1.6.0.post1 and cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0; the libraries the cu11 Aer wheel links) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268806882,"data":"| cutensor-cu11 | 2.2.0 (the newest release inside cutensornet-cu11 2.5.0's `\u003e=2.0.1,\u003c3`) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268811675,"data":"| qiskit-ibm-runtime | 0.50.0 (fake backends such as FakeFez; no account or credential) | PyPI |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268816279,"data":"| hypercomplex, hypercomplex-engine, hypercomplex-algebra, Cayley-Calculator, octonion, mathdunders | 0.3.4, 0.5.0, 0.2.0.2, 1.3.1, 0.1.0, 0.4.2 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268820621,"data":"| quaternionic, clifford, kingdon, galgebra, pyoctonion | 1.0.18, 1.5.1, 3.0.0, 0.6.0, 3.12 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26882483,"data":"| pyquaternion | 0.9.9 | PyPI sdist, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe (writes the VERSION.txt the sdist omits) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268828892,"data":"| cayley-dickson, SplitOct | commits abf96e7, e29e72f | GitHub archive, sha256-pinned, PKGBUILD recipe |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268832987,"data":"| hyprat | 0.2.0 | GitHub tag archive, sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268836829,"data":"| Octonion-Sedenion | 1.0.0 | PyPI wheel (its only release form), sha256-pinned |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268840955,"data":"| numpy-quaternion | 2024.0.13 | PyPI compiled wheel at the pin; `--extract` binds its Python files to the sha256-pinned sdist (Octonion-Sedenion builds on it) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268845321,"data":"| numba, sparse, anywidget | 0.68.0, 0.17.0, 0.11.0 | PyPI (`RUNTIME_PINS`; runtime dependencies of quaternionic, clifford and kingdon) |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268850569,"data":"| numpy, scipy, sympy, pandas, torch | Kaggle image versions, recorded per run | Kaggle image |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268906901,"data":"| SageMath | 10.10 | build host only; a computation that needs Sage stays there |\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268911599,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268915263,"data":"## Rules\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268919014,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268922595,"data":"- A kernel is private, has internet enabled (and a GPU when one is\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268926609,"data":"  requested), and holds no IBM credential. Noise comes from a retained\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268930491,"data":"  `gororoba_quantum/calibration_snapshot.py` export.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268934392,"data":"- The entry reads `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE`, which the kernel sets to its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268943021,"data":"  machine's device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268947223,"data":"- An output is a numerical simulation. It enters\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268950981,"data":"  `docs/state/research_state.json` only after a CPU replay gate re-derives\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268955095,"data":"  a reduced case.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26896103,"data":"- The push selects hardware with `--accelerator`; `environment.json`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268970392,"data":"  records what actually ran.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268988028,"data":"- Measured limits of each machine shape, the qubit size guide and the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268992388,"data":"  captured Kaggle documentation are in `docs/notes/kaggle/`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.268997029,"data":"- An entry whose output a CI gate recompiles runs with `push --ci-env` on a\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269001313,"data":"  CPU or GPU machine, using CPU Aer either way. The kernel then builds CI's Python 3.14.7 with CI's pins\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269006198,"data":"  through `ci/install_pins.sh` and runs the entry under it, because the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269010655,"data":"  image's Python 3.13 and numpy 2.1.3 change compiled depths and durations.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269014649,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269018297,"data":"## Aer on the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269022144,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269025759,"data":"- **Requesting a GPU.** Push with `--machine NvidiaTeslaT4` and a `--timeout`\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269029747,"data":"  sized to the work; kaggle_run.py refuses an accelerator push without one.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269033735,"data":"  The kernel installs qiskit-aer-gpu-cu11 0.17.2, cuquantum-cu11 24.8.0 and\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269037628,"data":"  cutensor-cu11 2.2.0 and sets `GOROROBA_AER_DEVICE=GPU`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269041568,"data":"- **cuStateVec.** `noise_simulator(..., custatevec=True)`, or\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269045398,"data":"  `GOROROBA_AER_CUSTATEVEC=1` in the entry's environment, sets\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269049268,"data":"  `cuStateVec_enable` on a GPU statevector or density-matrix run; `scripts/aer_gpu_probe.py\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269053305,"data":"  --workloads n21 --configurations\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269057094,"data":"  cpu_statevector,gpu_statevector_unbatched,gpu_statevector_custatevec` records\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269061075,"data":"  the three paths with Aer's reported `cuStateVec_enable`. The option excludes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269067032,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`. `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` holds the library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269075483,"data":"  chain, the T4 push command and how to read its result.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26909312,"data":"- **Pinned GPU environment.** A push with `--gpu-env` runs the entry in\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26909863,"data":"  /tmp/gororoba/gpu-venv:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269104122999998,"data":"  - The venv runs the image's Python with the repository's pins and the GPU\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269108695,"data":"    Aer wheels in qiskit-aer's place.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269118761,"data":"  - Before the entry, gpu_env.json records each pin's installed version, the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269127001,"data":"    owners of `qiskit_aer/__init__.py`, Aer's devices, and two seeded Bell\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269171318,"data":"    runs on the GPU.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269180755,"data":"  - A nonempty `failures` list stops the kernel with exit 4, before the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269184623,"data":"    entry starts. Each failure names what to fix:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269188273,"data":"    - a pin that resolved to another version;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26920902,"data":"    - a CPU qiskit-aer that shares the qiskit_aer/ files;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269214032,"data":"    - a GPU that nvidia-smi does not list;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269218799,"data":"    - a Bell run that raised, ran on another device, or left cuStateVec off;\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269223606,"data":"    - on a `--gpu-aer cu13` push (spec `cuda_in_venv`), a mapped CUDA library\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269228415,"data":"      other than the driver's libcuda.so from outside the venv, or no mapped\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269232209,"data":"      CUDA library at all.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269236035,"data":"  - `push --gpu-env-with torch` adds torch 2.14.1, the build host's version,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269239898,"data":"    to the venv's pins, so a torch entry runs over the repository's numpy\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269243779,"data":"    and qiskit instead of the image's; the preflight requires it at that\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269247776,"data":"    version like every other pin.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26925163,"data":"  - Under `--gpu-aer cu13` the Aer wheel comes from an attached dataset:\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269255619,"data":"    gpu_env.json's `wheel` names the file found under /kaggle/input and its\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269259632,"data":"    sha256, and a missing or different file is a failure before any install.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269263576,"data":"    The report's `controller_wrappers` and `cuda_libraries` show where each\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269267498,"data":"    CUDA library resolved.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26931043,"data":"  - Read gpu-env-report.txt and install-pins.txt in the output for the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269316115,"data":"    commands' own output.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269320883,"data":"  - \"Keeping the run on the GPU\" in `docs/notes/kaggle/custatevec.md` maps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269325959,"data":"    each route to the CPU to the check that closes it.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269330583,"data":"- **Using it in an entry.** The entry passes\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269334498,"data":"  `calibration_snapshot.aer_device()` to `noise_simulator(snapshot, device,\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.2693384,"data":"  method=...)`. On a GPU the simulator batches shots of circuits of at most\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269342383,"data":"  10 active qubits without control flow and runs feed-forward circuits shot\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269346285,"data":"  by shot (`calibration_snapshot.SnapshotSimulator`).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269350235,"data":"- **Noise model width.** Restricting the snapshot and the circuit to the\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269355437,"data":"  active qubits (`snapshot_laws.restrict` and `restrict_circuit`) keeps\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269364818,"data":"  Aer's noise model at the circuit's width on either device.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26936889,"data":"- **What the GPU is for.** It pays for density matrices at\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269372839,"data":"  `local_compute.GPU_MIN_ACTIVE_QUBITS` (11) qubits or more and for wide\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26937687,"data":"  statevectors. Small dynamic circuits sample faster on the host CPUs. On\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269380618,"data":"  the 7-qubit N=21 order-finding circuits, statevector trajectories took 2.8\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269384813,"data":"  and 36 ms per shot on the CPU, against 21.7 and 54.6 ms on one T4.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269388652,"data":"- **Batched shots.** `noise_simulator(..., batched_shots=True)` enables Aer's\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269394661,"data":"  `batched_shots_gpu`, which aborts on any circuit with control flow\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269398727,"data":"  (`if_else` lowers to `jump`), so only static circuits may batch. Batched\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269404743,"data":"  static runs are unmeasured here.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269409104,"data":"- **Replay.** A GPU's seeded counts differ from the CPU's. Its records are\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.26941399,"data":"  replayed from their retained counts, never by resampling on CI.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269419038,"data":"\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269424217,"data":"The measurements are in `docs/notes/kaggle/substrates.md`, from\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269428966,"data":"`results/kaggle/2026-10-16T204620Z-gororoba-aer-gpu-probe`.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":16.269432966,"data":"\n"}
